WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.584 --> 00:00:11.466
(Singing) I am an endangered species

00:00:11.466 --> 00:00:13.510
(Applause and cheers)

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:19.933
But I sing no victim song.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.853
I am a woman.

00:00:23.895 --> 00:00:27.357
I am an artist.

00:00:28.149 --> 00:00:35.031
And I know

00:00:35.031 --> 00:00:40.829
where my voice ...

00:00:41.621 --> 00:00:45.500
belongs.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:51.965
(Applause and cheers)

00:00:52.507 --> 00:00:56.261
Now, you might have heard
me sing that song.

00:00:57.095 --> 00:01:00.348
It was September 12th, 2022,

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:06.187
right after Amy Poehler
and Seth Meyers said,

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:09.065
"And the winner is,

00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:12.777
Sheryl Lee Ralph!"

00:01:12.819 --> 00:01:14.195
What!?

00:01:15.363 --> 00:01:18.992
I had just won the Emmy Award

00:01:19.034 --> 00:01:22.412
for Best Supporting Actress in a comedy

00:01:22.454 --> 00:01:26.666
for my role as Mrs. Barbara Howard

00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:31.588
on your favorite TV show,
"Abbott Elementary."

00:01:31.588 --> 00:01:33.423
(Cheers)

00:01:33.423 --> 00:01:35.133
Oh, yes.

00:01:35.175 --> 00:01:37.761
And I was shocked.

00:01:38.678 --> 00:01:43.892
As the children would say,
shooketh into disbelief.

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:49.189
Oh, my goodness, it was my first time
at the Emmys and I won.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:51.274
Yes!

00:01:51.274 --> 00:01:54.194
And I got to tell you,

00:01:54.194 --> 00:01:56.363
in that moment,

00:01:56.404 --> 00:02:00.742
I was so stunned into disbelief

00:02:00.784 --> 00:02:03.912
that I don't know
how I got up on the stage.

00:02:05.455 --> 00:02:11.044
There I was, just listening
to that roar of applause.

00:02:11.044 --> 00:02:12.629
Mm mm mm.

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:16.091
And my whole career flashed
right there in front of me.

00:02:16.091 --> 00:02:22.097
Starting with 19-year-old Sheryl Lee
in her first movie

00:02:22.138 --> 00:02:27.018
being directed
by the great Sidney Poitier.

00:02:27.936 --> 00:02:29.562
Oh, yeah, you can clap that.

00:02:29.604 --> 00:02:32.732
(Applause)

00:02:32.732 --> 00:02:38.321
Followed by ten years
of “no” after “no” after “no.”

00:02:39.572 --> 00:02:42.283
Before the next film role came about.

00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:45.495
But I filled in that time with TV

00:02:45.537 --> 00:02:48.331
and more "nos" and more rejection

00:02:48.373 --> 00:02:52.711
until I made it big on Broadway

00:02:52.752 --> 00:02:58.216
in what has become
the iconic musical of the '80s,

00:02:58.258 --> 00:02:59.843
because I say so,

00:02:59.884 --> 00:03:00.969
(Laughter)

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.762
"Dreamgirls."

00:03:02.762 --> 00:03:05.056
(Applause)

00:03:05.098 --> 00:03:08.935
And boy, did I learn a lot
of life lessons there.

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:15.692
And I mean, after so many
moments of doubt, disbelief,

00:03:15.692 --> 00:03:19.904
there I was, on that Emmy stage,

00:03:19.904 --> 00:03:23.742
with this huge sign
in front of me flashing

00:03:23.783 --> 00:03:27.203
"Stop now," "Stop now," "Stop now."

00:03:27.245 --> 00:03:28.580
And I started to think,

00:03:28.621 --> 00:03:32.751
“My God, what if I had stopped
after all of those ‘nos?’

00:03:32.792 --> 00:03:37.130
What if I had stopped after all of those
moments of feeling defeated?

00:03:37.172 --> 00:03:39.507
What if I had stopped?"

00:03:40.425 --> 00:03:43.762
I wouldn't be standing there

00:03:43.803 --> 00:03:46.681
for that golden moment.

00:03:48.308 --> 00:03:50.518
But right now,

00:03:50.518 --> 00:03:53.897
many of us, we are feeling ...

00:03:55.857 --> 00:03:58.485
deeply challenged

00:03:58.526 --> 00:04:00.528
trying to hold on

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.697
and believe in ourselves,

00:04:02.697 --> 00:04:05.492
and I do not mean in a toxic way.

00:04:05.533 --> 00:04:10.205
I am talking about a way
that comes from confidence,

00:04:10.205 --> 00:04:14.751
the kind of confidence
that can keep us moving forward

00:04:14.793 --> 00:04:17.712
when we are feeling

00:04:17.754 --> 00:04:21.674
like we are carrying
the weight of the pandemic,

00:04:21.716 --> 00:04:25.970
trying to figure out
all of this political division,

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:32.769
fighting all of the mental, physical,
social violence in our homes,

00:04:32.769 --> 00:04:35.188
in our communities,

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:38.817
to climate change, social media.

00:04:39.192 --> 00:04:41.069
It's a lot.

00:04:42.195 --> 00:04:47.700
Making it hard to believe
in the goodness in the world.

00:04:48.827 --> 00:04:55.792
And harder still to believe
in the goodness of ourselves.

00:04:56.626 --> 00:05:02.173
This is a rough time, people,
and our mental health is suffering.

00:05:02.215 --> 00:05:05.802
We all need a checkup from the neck up.

00:05:05.844 --> 00:05:07.846
(Laughter)

00:05:07.887 --> 00:05:09.722
And I don't mean -- yeah, it's OK.

00:05:09.764 --> 00:05:11.307
You feel me, thank you.

00:05:11.349 --> 00:05:12.642
(Applause)

00:05:12.642 --> 00:05:16.020
And I don't mean just medicine.

00:05:16.855 --> 00:05:23.278
I actually mean reframing our thinking

00:05:23.319 --> 00:05:29.409
of our ability to believe in ourselves.

00:05:30.618 --> 00:05:32.245
Now I know,

00:05:32.245 --> 00:05:37.750
you see me on TV, in magazines,
on movie screens,

00:05:37.792 --> 00:05:39.627
and you might be thinking to yourself,

00:05:39.627 --> 00:05:44.465
"What does she know about struggling
to believe in herself?"

00:05:44.507 --> 00:05:46.467
Well, let me tell you something.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.262
I do not look like my journey.

00:05:49.762 --> 00:05:51.472
(Laughter)

00:05:51.472 --> 00:05:57.270
(Applause)

00:05:57.312 --> 00:06:00.273
Oh, I've been through a few things.

00:06:00.648 --> 00:06:04.068
And the struggle is real.

00:06:04.986 --> 00:06:08.907
But I have learned something in my life.

00:06:09.365 --> 00:06:13.953
That there are three things
that we all must do

00:06:13.953 --> 00:06:18.207
in order to believe in ourselves.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:20.418
Number one.

00:06:21.252 --> 00:06:24.714
First, we need to see ourselves.

00:06:24.756 --> 00:06:27.508
I mean, really, truly,

00:06:27.508 --> 00:06:33.556
deeply see ourselves
for who and what we are

00:06:33.556 --> 00:06:36.225
in order to believe in ourselves.

00:06:36.976 --> 00:06:40.897
I’m a child of the ’60s,
and that was hard.

00:06:41.814 --> 00:06:43.191
Oh.

00:06:43.191 --> 00:06:45.360
In the third grade,

00:06:45.401 --> 00:06:50.698
I tested out of public school
into a fancy private school

00:06:51.199 --> 00:06:57.538
where the only Black person
I saw every day

00:06:57.538 --> 00:07:02.210
was the one who looked back
at me in the mirror.

00:07:03.419 --> 00:07:08.549
I was by myself, and I was all alone.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:13.846
And the things that were said to me,

00:07:13.888 --> 00:07:16.808
and I'm not talking about just the kids,

00:07:16.808 --> 00:07:19.060
but the adults, too.

00:07:19.811 --> 00:07:25.233
And when I would come home
from school crying the ugly cry,

00:07:25.233 --> 00:07:31.656
my immigrant Jamaican mother
would sit me down in front of the mirror

00:07:31.698 --> 00:07:33.741
and ask me,

00:07:33.783 --> 00:07:36.786
"Do you see an N-word?

00:07:37.203 --> 00:07:39.956
Do you see a liar?

00:07:40.289 --> 00:07:44.127
Do you see a big-lip monkey?

00:07:44.127 --> 00:07:45.545
No!

00:07:45.586 --> 00:07:47.338
So dry your eyes.

00:07:47.338 --> 00:07:51.092
And when you go back to school, remember,

00:07:51.092 --> 00:07:52.927
you are rubber,

00:07:52.927 --> 00:07:54.887
they are glue.

00:07:54.929 --> 00:07:59.100
And every ignorant thing
they say about you

00:07:59.142 --> 00:08:03.021
bounces off of you and sticks to them."

00:08:03.396 --> 00:08:10.028
(Applause)

00:08:10.486 --> 00:08:12.655
And I believed her.

00:08:13.364 --> 00:08:15.199
And it didn't hurt.

00:08:15.908 --> 00:08:17.035
So much.

00:08:18.244 --> 00:08:20.371
Because I believed.

00:08:21.539 --> 00:08:22.665
Number two.

00:08:24.542 --> 00:08:26.502
We've got to think.

00:08:26.919 --> 00:08:31.632
Think about ourselves
in order to believe in ourselves.

00:08:31.632 --> 00:08:35.803
Growing up, my dad had a sign on his desk.

00:08:35.845 --> 00:08:38.931
And it said, "Think."

00:08:39.724 --> 00:08:41.017
"Think."

00:08:41.392 --> 00:08:46.439
Oh, I did not know
how valuable and powerful

00:08:46.481 --> 00:08:48.983
the simple act of thinking was

00:08:48.983 --> 00:08:54.572
until I came back to Hollywood
from my triumphant run on Broadway,

00:08:54.614 --> 00:09:00.578
and I had this meeting with a big studio
Hollywood casting director.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:02.455
Oh, I was so excited.

00:09:02.497 --> 00:09:06.334
I walked in and he looked
at me and he said,

00:09:06.375 --> 00:09:07.835
"Hm.

00:09:07.877 --> 00:09:11.255
Everybody knows you're a beautiful,
talented Black girl.

00:09:11.839 --> 00:09:17.095
But what do I do with a beautiful,
talented Black girl?

00:09:17.678 --> 00:09:21.516
Do I put you in a movie with Tom Cruise?

00:09:21.974 --> 00:09:24.018
Does he kiss you? Ugh.

00:09:25.269 --> 00:09:28.147
Who goes to see that movie?"

00:09:32.235 --> 00:09:33.402
(Laughs)

00:09:35.071 --> 00:09:37.657
I could not believe

00:09:37.698 --> 00:09:43.996
that that man had just said that
to me, to my face.

00:09:44.497 --> 00:09:46.290
And he hurt me.

00:09:46.874 --> 00:09:48.835
He hurt me so deeply,

00:09:48.876 --> 00:09:51.754
I was actually thinking about quitting.

00:09:53.923 --> 00:09:55.800
Until ...

00:09:56.551 --> 00:09:58.845
I started to think.

00:09:59.887 --> 00:10:01.889
And I thought about what he said.

00:10:01.931 --> 00:10:04.892
He said that everybody knew

00:10:04.934 --> 00:10:08.563
that I was a beautiful,
talented Black girl.

00:10:08.563 --> 00:10:09.772
(Laughter)

00:10:09.814 --> 00:10:15.486
(Cheers and applause)

00:10:15.486 --> 00:10:22.368
And that I deserve to be cast in movies
with the likes of Tom Cruise,

00:10:22.368 --> 00:10:24.328
and he should kiss me.

00:10:24.328 --> 00:10:26.664
(Applause)

00:10:26.706 --> 00:10:27.999
(Laughs)

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:33.045
So what was meant to break me
did not break me, it built me up.

00:10:33.087 --> 00:10:36.799
I believed that man,
I believed what he said.

00:10:36.799 --> 00:10:42.722
And I walked out of there giving myself
permission to take up space in Hollywood,

00:10:42.763 --> 00:10:44.432
knowing that I belonged there

00:10:44.473 --> 00:10:47.935
no matter what anybody thought about me.

00:10:48.561 --> 00:10:54.692
(Cheers and applause)

00:10:55.693 --> 00:10:56.903
Thirdly.

00:10:57.695 --> 00:11:02.408
We've got to act
like we believe in ourselves.

00:11:02.408 --> 00:11:03.618
Oh, yeah.

00:11:03.618 --> 00:11:06.621
Because when we believe
in ourselves and act on it,

00:11:06.662 --> 00:11:11.000
we create possibilities
that never would have been possible

00:11:11.042 --> 00:11:14.503
had we not just believed.

00:11:14.879 --> 00:11:18.341
OK, so I will tell you another story.

00:11:19.217 --> 00:11:23.638
I will never forget walking into one
of those crowded Hollywood rooms,

00:11:23.679 --> 00:11:28.059
and I see Harry Thomason,
producer Harry Thomason,

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:31.687
who is married to Linda
Bloodworth-Thomason,

00:11:31.687 --> 00:11:35.399
writer, creator of the series
"Designing Women."

00:11:36.442 --> 00:11:39.487
I walk right up to Harry and I say,

00:11:39.528 --> 00:11:42.657
"How can it be,
that after all of these years

00:11:42.698 --> 00:11:47.078
Anthony has not had
a relationship with a Black woman?

00:11:47.578 --> 00:11:52.250
After all, the show
takes place in Atlanta,

00:11:52.291 --> 00:11:53.501
Georgia."

00:11:53.542 --> 00:11:56.212
(Laughter)

00:11:56.629 --> 00:12:00.174
He looked at me, took a step back

00:12:00.174 --> 00:12:02.677
and said, "Who are you?"

00:12:03.469 --> 00:12:06.055
I said, "I'm Sheryl Lee Ralph."

00:12:06.055 --> 00:12:09.725
And he said, "OK.

00:12:09.767 --> 00:12:12.687
Have your people call my people

00:12:12.728 --> 00:12:15.773
and we will see what we can do."

00:12:17.233 --> 00:12:18.985
And guess what happened?

00:12:19.026 --> 00:12:20.403
(Laughter)

00:12:20.403 --> 00:12:25.283
I got cast as Etienne Toussaint Bouvier,

00:12:25.324 --> 00:12:29.370
Las Vegas showgirl turned Anthony's wife

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:33.249
for the final season of "Designing Women."

00:12:33.291 --> 00:12:34.667
(Cheers and applause)

00:12:34.709 --> 00:12:35.960
Oh, yeah.

00:12:36.919 --> 00:12:40.298
Against all odds, once again,

00:12:40.339 --> 00:12:45.094
I gave myself permission to take up space,

00:12:45.094 --> 00:12:48.055
believing that I belonged.

00:12:48.055 --> 00:12:54.562
I believed that if Sheryl Lee
did the work of honing her craft,

00:12:54.562 --> 00:12:57.398
building solid relationships

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:01.235
and stayed ready
so she didn't have to get ready,

00:13:01.277 --> 00:13:04.113
anything was possible.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.658
Heck, winning an Emmy.

00:13:08.701 --> 00:13:09.869
A Grammy.

00:13:10.619 --> 00:13:11.787
An Oscar.

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:13.706
A Tony.

00:13:13.748 --> 00:13:16.125
EGOT it, baby.

00:13:16.167 --> 00:13:18.419
(Cheering)

00:13:18.419 --> 00:13:19.670
So ...

00:13:20.546 --> 00:13:24.550
When you leave this room today,

00:13:24.592 --> 00:13:29.764
I challenge all of you
to start a meaningful practice

00:13:29.805 --> 00:13:32.099
of looking in the mirror

00:13:32.141 --> 00:13:34.185
and loving what you see.

00:13:34.643 --> 00:13:37.897
Believe in what you see.

00:13:38.731 --> 00:13:42.360
If you can't love it, then respect it.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:45.946
And if you can't respect it,
then encourage it.

00:13:45.988 --> 00:13:49.367
If you can't encourage it, empower it.

00:13:49.408 --> 00:13:56.374
And if you can't empower it,
please be kind to it.

00:13:57.124 --> 00:14:03.172
(Applause)

00:14:03.214 --> 00:14:07.760
The greatest relationship,

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:12.264
the greatest one you will ever have

00:14:12.306 --> 00:14:13.974
is with yourself.

00:14:15.017 --> 00:14:17.353
Believe me.

00:14:17.395 --> 00:14:20.272
Have faith in yourself.

00:14:20.272 --> 00:14:25.861
Believing that faith
can make broken wings fly.

00:14:25.903 --> 00:14:30.032
And we deserve to soar.

00:14:31.951 --> 00:14:34.787
Remember,

00:14:34.829 --> 00:14:38.499
maybe one of these days
when you pass the mirror

00:14:38.499 --> 00:14:42.169
and you catch a glimpse of yourself,

00:14:42.169 --> 00:14:44.213
remember, I told you this.

00:14:44.797 --> 00:14:51.512
That is what believing looks like.

00:14:51.554 --> 00:14:55.099
And don't you ever, ever,

00:14:55.141 --> 00:14:59.979
ever give up on you.

00:15:00.604 --> 00:15:04.358
I am Sheryl Lee Ralph,

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:09.655
and I love you just the way you are.

00:15:09.697 --> 00:15:13.659
(Singing) Believe in yourself

00:15:13.659 --> 00:15:20.666
As I believe in you

00:15:23.169 --> 00:15:24.753
Thank you.

00:15:24.795 --> 00:15:31.719
(Cheers and applause)

